"""HP EliteBook thermal profile: the daemon and its command line.

``elitebook-thermal-profile daemon`` is the systemd service and the only
process that writes power settings (see elitebook_engine). Every other
command is a client: profile names and ``auto`` ask the daemon over a root-only
Unix socket, ``status`` reads the state files, and ``apply-once`` runs a
single reconcile pass without a daemon, for tests and for rescue when the
service cannot start.

The command line, state files and warning texts match the dispatcher this
replaced, so the GNOME extension and the power guard keep working unchanged.
Standard library only.
"""

